- label: live detection covers every process-backed agent CLI, not only claude: findLiveAgentSessions probes codex (binary codex), cursor (cursor-agent), factory (droid), and opencode (opencode) with per-binary pgrep — an exact-name -x invocation plus an anchored full-argv -f pattern '(^|/)<binary>($| )' because cursor-agent execs node with a renamed argv[0] and npm launchers hide the real binary name, with -a prepended on darwin per the same BSD ancestor rule as findLiveClaude — resolves ALL matched pids' working directories in ONE batched procCwds probe, dedupes (source, cwd) pairs, and maps each pair to that agent's newest recording; process presence in a cwd that has a recording is a candidate only (never sufficient for live), because an idle-open TUI holds no generating turn, so open-fd probing alone can never see these CLIs and process+cwd alone must not mark them RUNNING
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'findLiveAgentSessions|agentPgrepInvocations|per-agent process' test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js test/sessions/live-sessions-platform.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, implemented]
- label: each live (source, cwd) pair resolves to a session path by the source's own storage layout: codex takes the newest discovered codex session whose first-line session_meta cwd EQUALS the probed cwd (candidates prefiltered by project label, first-line reads bounded to a fixed cap, mtime-descending so the running session wins), cursor scans ~/.cursor/projects/<slug>/agent-transcripts for the newest <uuid>/<uuid>.jsonl where slug is the cwd with its leading slash dropped and every '/' replaced by '-', factory scans ~/.factory/sessions/ws<slug> root-level .jsonl where slug is the cwd with every '/' replaced by '-' (matching the observed and fixture layouts), and opencode takes the newest discovered opencode:// session whose project label equals shortenProjectPath(cwd) — an agent process whose cwd has no recording contributes nothing, and every resolver degrades to empty on missing dirs or unreadable files without throwing
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'maps to the newest|session_meta cwd equals|cwd has no recording contributes nothing' test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, implemented]
- label: detectLiveSessions unions FOUR detection families under the one 5s memo — findLiveGrok (active_sessions.json + pid cwd match + generating turn), findLiveClaude (pgrep + project-dir newest + not idle), findLiveAgentSessions (per-agent process candidates for codex/cursor/factory/opencode filtered to generating recordings), and findLiveByOpenFd over recent-mtime codex/cursor/factory candidates that are still generating (extra recall for an agent caught mid-write; a completed idle jsonl that is merely held open is not live) — while cursor-cloud is deliberately and honestly ABSENT from every family: a cloud agent has no local process to probe, so an imported cursor-cloud recording is never reported live no matter how recent its mtime, rather than faking a RUNNING state from import freshness
  id: r23
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'detectLiveSessions|cursor-cloud is never|unions' test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, implemented]
- label: the launched-run identity badge #runStatus on /run?id= uses the same generating bit as detectLiveSessions / runIsLive(), never tmux status === running: runPage() SSR and setStatus after snapshot poll paint idle for an idle launched G1 window (tmux running, recording settled, not in the live set) and running for a generating launched G2 window (same tmux running, recording in detectLiveSessions); updateHeaderIdentity paints #runStatus from runIsLive (not only id/model/stats/grade); exited/gone still come from pane death; the raw-terminal data-status may stay pane-alive
  id: d1rs
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: the launched-run chat on /run?id= uses the same generating bit as detectLiveSessions / runIsLive() for #composerStatus, GET /api/runs/session status, and activityHtml: runPage() SSR and session-poll applySession paint #composerStatus data-state idle (not Running with Stop) for an idle launched G1 window (tmux running, recording settled, not in the live set) and running for a generating launched G2 window; GET /api/runs and GET /api/runs/session status/state is running (generating, including no sessionPath yet) | idle (linked but not generating) | exited (pane dead), never running merely because sessionPath exists or the tmux pane is alive; activityHtml shows Thinking / Planning next moves only while generating, not for idle G1
  id: d1ca
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "D1" test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js test/routes/launch-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: GET /api/runs, GET /api/runs/session, and GET /api/runs/snapshot use one generating bit and one word: status is running only while the launched run is generating (no sessionPath yet, or linked recording in detectLiveSessions / runIsLive), idle for an idle launched G1 window (tmux pane-alive, recording settled, not in the live set), and exited when the pane is dead — never tmux-alive as status running. /api/runs and /api/runs/session state equals that same status (running|idle|exited), not a sidecar live vs running split. /run?id= identity #runStatus and composer follow that status field.
  id: d1pw
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js test/routes/launch-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: the /view run chip and GET /api/sessions/live nested run.status use the same generating bit as GET /api/runs*: an idle launched G1 window (tmux pane-alive, recording settled, not in detectLiveSessions) paints idle run · open chat and run.status idle, a generating launched G2 window paints running run · open chat and run.status running, and a dead pane stays exited — never live/running merely because the tmux pane is alive. runGeneratingStatus is the one server mapping shared with poll APIs and /run?id= SSR. /api/sessions/live state is that same generating word (running|idle), never state live beside run.status running
  id: d1vs
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/launch-page.test.js test/routes/session-live-routes.test.js test/routes/route-handlers-pages.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: the /view external watch chip uses the same generating words running|idle|exited as the launched-run chip: a generating external session (detectLiveSessions member, no run window) paints running session · open chat with data-status=running on the chip and chip-dot targeting /run?session=<hash>, never live session · watch live and never the word live in chip copy; a not-live external session still gets no watch chip; the run chip still wins when a window is linked
  id: d1wc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'live watch chip|D1' test/routes/route-handlers-pages.test.js test/browser/launch-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: GET /run?session= destination copy uses the same generating words running|idle as the /view chip that opens it — never live session: a generating session titles "tracequest — running session <hash>", paints observer heading "Watching a running session", and empty-transcript "the agent process is running but this recording has no turns"; an idle session titles "tracequest — idle session <hash>" and observer heading "Watching an idle session" (never Watching a live session); 404 uses kicker "session watch" not "live session watch"; dashboard external row ariaLabel is Watch running session, never Watch live session
  id: d1wp
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1' test/browser/run-page.test.js test/routes/route-handlers-pages.test.js test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: leftover user-visible live-session copy is gone from the dashboard row and /run destinations: idle G1 observer paragraph does not say "The transcript updates live as the agent works" (idle observer-note says the agent is not generating right now; generating hidden observer-note says the transcript updates as the agent works, never live); dashboard external origin chip title does not say "Detected live session" (it explains started outside tracequest, matching the destination origin chip); /run?id= model chip title does not say "Model reported by the live session recording" (it says session recording); palette this-chat fallback subtitle is Open chat, never Watch live — those leftover phrases are banned on the served HTML
  id: d1lx
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1' test/browser/run-page.test.js test/routes/route-handlers-pages.test.js test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js test/browser/command-palette-nav.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: GET /run?session= idle G1 inside QUIET_MS paints a completed idle column, not a generating trail: growth lastState follows identity (idle, not deriveWatchLive etag inside 4s), containNamedOutput leftover-snaps (does not park named-output), activityHtml does not emit shimmering Planning next moves, #liveTailForm is hidden, and the visible composer is #continueForm placeholder Send a follow-up (not Stop)
  id: d1ic
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1: idle G1 /run.session= #runStatus stays idle inside QUIET_MS|quiet-window|quiet.window' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: GET /run?session= idle G1 leftover-occupies leftover with BAR named shell-output column leftover-owned pixels in production leftover: leftoverSnapIsStale does not treat G1 real tool-then-prose (opening prose, named shell output, closing prose) as after-growth; first-turn production containNamedOutput leftover-occupies leftover viewport (flex:1 leftover, leftover.bottom is composer.top of leftover.clientHeight leftover viewport, leftover = composer.top − leftover.top = leftover.clientHeight) with leftover-owned pixels opening prose + named card (Lines 1-6, fillLeftover, data-contained !== parked, not split into #chatHistory) + closing prose occupying leftover — leftover layout takes user + prior lsof/ps dumps off leftover; leftoverAir is leftover − leftoverOwned (BAR leftover has leftover air under closing; leftover occupancy of leftover-owned content is not leftover occupancy of leftover; leftover is not leftoverOwned; leftoverAir is not required ≤ 8); leftover bounds are production leftover leftover viewport, never leftover occupancy of leftover-owned content as leftover occupancy of leftover, never hardcoded 0-560 leftover box, never occupancy only a named card flag; tests run production leftover layout (production rerender + applyThreadItems + production containNamedOutput) on the real G1 fixture — never stub leftoverSnapIsStale/rerender/snapNamedOutputCard occupancy, never helper-bake fold captions, never a tool-less assistant, never pre-bake leftover occupancy
  id: d1ns
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1: idle G1 /run.session= #runStatus stays idle inside QUIET_MS|quiet-window|quiet.window|leftoverSnapIsStale' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
# live-sessions
- label: live-session process probing is platform-abstracted in src/sessions/proc-probe.js: procCwds(pids) resolves per-pid working directories and openPathsAmong(paths) reports which candidate session files are held open, with a readlink /proc implementation on linux and an lsof implementation on darwin, selected by process.platform and overridable per call for tests
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/sessions/live-sessions-platform.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, implemented]
- label: procCwds accepts only strictly numeric pids (active_sessions.json is user-writable and lsof -p rejects an entire comma-joined list containing one non-numeric entry); lsof output is parsed as NUL-delimited -F0 fields, and on darwin candidate paths are additionally indexed under lsof's escaped rendering (two-character escapes for backslash/newline/CR/tab/backspace/formfeed, caret notation for other C0 controls, \x7f for DEL) so session files containing those characters are still matched
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'malformed pid|escaped form|escapes backslash|every character class|not registered on the linux' test/sessions/live-sessions-platform.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, implemented]
- label: findLiveClaude passes -a to pgrep on darwin because BSD pgrep omits its own ancestors by default, which would hide the very claude session that launched tracequest; linux omits -a, where the flag instead means --list-full and would break pid parsing
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'pgrep does not hide|omit -a|platform-correct args|BSD pgrep really' test/sessions/live-sessions-platform.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, implemented]
- label: a session is live only while that session's agent is currently generating a response or executing tools for it: process-alive plus cwd-match is never sufficient, so an attached idle TUI (Grok G1 at Send a follow-up after a completed assistant turn, Claude status idle / end_turn, and idle-open Codex/Cursor/Factory/OpenCode recordings) is not a member of detectLiveSessions even when the process is still listed in active_sessions.json or pgrep
  id: lofp
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, idle-open, implemented]
- label: findLiveGrok treats active_sessions.json plus a live pid whose cwd matches as a candidate only: the grok session dir is live when events.jsonl has an unmatched turn_started, chat_history has unmatched tool_calls, or a subagent meta.json status is running, and is not live when the last events record is turn_ended completed with no running subagent
  id: logk
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'G1|G2|G3|G4|findLiveGrok' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, idle-open, implemented]
- label: findLiveClaude does not report an idle-open Claude TUI as live: a ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json sidecar with status idle is not live only when the newest project jsonl is also settled (last assistant stop_reason end_turn, with turn_duration / away_summary); unmatched tool_use or a jsonl that has not closed the turn remains live even if the sidecar says idle
  id: locl
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'C1|C2|findLiveClaude' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, idle-open, implemented]
- label: findLiveAgentSessions does not treat process presence in a cwd that has a recording as live by itself: an idle-open Codex rollout (settled task, no pending custom_tool_call), Cursor transcript ending in turn_ended success, Factory jsonl whose last assistant turn is complete, or OpenCode session whose last message is complete is not live, while unmatched task_started / pending tools / missing turn_ended / in-progress last message stay live; a dead process or a cwd with no recording still contributes nothing
  id: loag
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'X1|findLiveAgentSessions' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, idle-open, implemented]
- label: the live bit is one vocabulary: for a mixed snapshot of an idle-open G1 grok session and a generating G2 grok session, session.live equals detectLiveSessions membership of session.path, and cursor-cloud remains never-live even with recent mtime and a held-open fd
  id: lod1
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1|CC ' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, idle-open, implemented]
- label: findLiveGrok reports a process-matched grok session live for in-flight generating: unmatched turn_started (including when that start has aged out of the 128KB tail and recent records are paired tools), unmatched chat_history tool_calls (including when that last record exceeds the 128KB tail), unmatched events tool_started, live phase after the last turn boundary, running subagent meta.json, in-progress reasoning, empty streaming assistant, last chat_history user waiting for the model, updates.jsonl agent_message_chunk or pending tool_call even after events turn_ended, or a jsonl file whose last line is incomplete (growing mid-write)
  id: ifgk
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'G2|in-flight grok' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, in-flight, implemented]
- label: findLiveClaude reports a process-matched Claude recording live while generating: unmatched tool_use (including when that last record exceeds the 128KB tail), last assistant without end_turn, last user waiting for the model, a non-idle pid sidecar status, or an incomplete last jsonl line, including when ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json has status idle — sidecar idle is not an absolute veto
  id: ifcl
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'C2|in-flight claude' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, in-flight, implemented]
- label: findLiveAgentSessions reports generating Codex/Cursor/Factory/OpenCode recordings live: unmatched task_started (including when that start has aged out of the 128KB tail and recent records are completed tools), pending custom_tool_call, trailing reasoning without task_complete, or incomplete last line (codex); missing turn_ended or incomplete last line (cursor); unmatched tool_use, last user, or incomplete last line (factory); last user, in-progress tool part, last-assistant streaming text (no step-finish / still-open text / message not completed), unmatched step-start, or empty assistant parts (opencode)
  id: ifag
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'X1b|X1d|X1f|X1h|in-flight' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, in-flight, implemented]
- label: openCodeSessionIsGenerating reports a process-matched OpenCode last assistant live while that turn is in-flight: streaming text without a finished step (no step-finish, still-open text/reasoning part, or message time.completed/finish unset), last user, empty assistant parts, unmatched step-start, or a non-completed tool part; a last assistant with time.completed or finish and paired step-finish is not live even with a live opencode pid
  id: ifoc
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'X1g|X1h' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, in-flight, implemented]
- label: the live bit is one vocabulary: detectLiveSessions membership, /api/sessions live, the dashboard list-row running badge, and CLI --filter live:true agree for the same snapshot — a path is live on every surface iff it is in detectLiveSessions; G1 idle-open is not live, G2 generating is live, G3 dead pid is not live, G4 cwd mismatch is not live, and cursor-cloud is never live even with recent mtime and a held-open fd
  id: d1sf
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1|G3|G4|CC |quiet.window|quiet-window' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js test/cli/cli-live-filter.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: the chat-page ~4s quiet-window / unmatched-tool_use live-tail heuristic (run-page.js QUIET_MS) is watch-page chrome only and must not promote an idle completed turn to a dashboard list-row RUNNING badge: renderRow and external live rows take live from s.live === true (the detectLiveSessions stamp), never from recording mtime recency or a hardcoded running status
  id: d1qw
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'quiet.window|quiet-window|D1: chat-page' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, chat-ui, implemented]
- label: detectLiveSessions does not treat an open fd on a recent-mtime codex/cursor/factory recording as live by itself: a completed idle jsonl that is merely held open (idle-open TUI, settled last record) is not a member of the live set even with a live agent pid/cwd, while an open-fd hit that is still generating (unmatched turn, pending tool, incomplete last line) remains extra mid-write recall
  id: lofd
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'X1a|X1c|X1e|held.open fd|idle-open Factory|factory source|open-fd live path|unions grok session' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/sessions/live-sessions.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, idle-open, implemented]
- label: claudeSessionIsGenerating does not treat ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json status idle as an absolute veto: a process-matched Claude jsonl that is generating (unmatched tool_use, last assistant without end_turn, last user waiting for the model, or incomplete last line) is live even when the pid sidecar says idle; sidecar idle is used only when the jsonl is also settled; a non-idle sidecar status remains a live shortcut for the first-token gap before jsonl writes
  id: ifci
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'C1|C2|idle sidecar' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, in-flight, implemented]
- label: dashboard RUNNING chrome is one driver: inventory live-indicator and page-1 external run-state-badge both read s.live === true only (never _livePaths membership, never a hardcoded status running), so a mixed G1-idle / G2-generating browserPage snapshot renders G2 as run-state-badge running and G1 with no running badge
  id: d1bd
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: one generating word running|idle|exited and one predicate (runIsLive is r.status === running, the same word runGeneratingStatus writes) drive list badges, /run?id= #runStatus/data-run-state/composer, /view chip copy, and /api/sessions/live state+run.status: a generating G2 is running on every surface, idle G1 is idle, never state live beside status running, never data-run-state live while #runStatus says running, never a live-run chip label on a running data-status, and runIsLive never AND-gates a second _liveSessions snapshot
  id: d1vo
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'D1' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js test/browser/run-page.test.js test/browser/launch-page.test.js test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js test/routes/session-live-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, surfaces, implemented]
- label: a process-matched Grok or Codex recording is live when the last 128KB tail has no closing boundary (no turn_ended / task_complete) even if the unmatched turn_started / task_started has aged out of that window and recent records are paired or completed tools — recordingIsGenerating must not require the opening token to still fit in TAIL_BYTES
  id: ifto
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'aged out of the 128KB tail' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, in-flight, implemented]
- label: grokSessionIsGenerating honors updates.jsonl agent_message_chunk / pending tool_call and a last chat_history user even when events.jsonl last boundary is turn_ended (first-token after a completed turn); a last updates turn_completed with settled events stays not-live so G1 idle-open is preserved
  id: ifgu
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'updates.jsonl|turn_completed is not live|last chat_history user after turn_ended' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, in-flight, implemented]
- label: readJsonlTail parses the last JSONL record even when that record exceeds the 128KB tail: a process-matched Claude unmatched tool_use last line of 143KB is live (C2), a process-matched Grok events turn_ended plus unmatched chat_history tool_calls last line of 143KB is live (G2), and an idle last record of the same size (Claude end_turn, Grok completed assistant) stays not-live — dropping the last line as empty objs must not classify generating as idle
  id: ifos
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'last record larger than the 128KB tail' test/sessions/live-sessions-finalisation.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-platform, in-flight, implemented]
